{# Feishu interactive-card helper macros (spec 10).

Each ``card_json.j2`` template builds an ``elements`` list of Feishu element
dicts directly (plain Python dicts accumulated via a ``namespace``), then calls
``card()`` once to render the full card document as JSON via ``tojson``. The
Feishu channel parses this JSON and POSTs it — the card has real ``hr`` /
``fields`` / ``action`` / ``card_link`` elements, not a flattened single div.

Element shapes (Feishu interactive card v1):
- ``{"tag": "div", "text": {"tag": "lark_md", "content": "..."}}`` — markdown block
- ``{"tag": "hr"}`` — horizontal rule
- ``{"tag": "div", "fields": [{...}, ...]}`` — each field ``{"is_short": true, "text": {...}}``
- ``{"tag": "action", "actions": [{"tag": "button", ...}]}`` — button row
- top-level ``"card_link": {"url": "..."}`` — makes the whole card clickable
#}

{# Render the final card document. ``elements`` is a list of element dicts. #}
{%- macro card(header_title, elements, markpost_url="") -%}
{%- set doc = {"config": {"wide_screen_mode": true}, "header": {"template": "blue", "title": {"tag": "plain_text", "content": header_title}}, "elements": elements} -%}
{%- if markpost_url -%}{%- set _ = doc.update({"card_link": {"url": markpost_url}}) -%}{%- endif -%}
{{ doc | tojson }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{# Build the markdown body for a titled repo list (top-5 + "... and N more").
   Returns a plain string, NOT JSON — wrap in a lark_md div by the caller. #}
{%- macro repo_list_content(title, repos) -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(lines=["**" ~ title ~ "**"]) -%}
{%- for name in repos[:5] -%}{%- set ns.lines = ns.lines + ["- " ~ name] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if repos | length > 5 -%}{%- set ns.lines = ns.lines + ["- ... and " ~ (repos | length - 5) ~ " more"] -%}{%- endif -%}
{{ ns.lines | join("\n") }}
{%- endmacro -%}
